-- title:
--   Monomial germs descend exactly through the tame cyclic quotient
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring and is adically complete for its maximal ideal), and let $\pi \in W$ generate the maximal ideal. Fix $m \ge 1$ and write $M =$ `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ m)`, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0,X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - \pi^m$, assumed to be local and adically complete for its maximal ideal; `const (π ^ m) w` denotes the class of the constant $w$, and `U (π ^ m)`, `V (π ^ m)` are the two distinguished branch parameters of $M$. Fix $n \ge 1$ with $n$ invertible in $W$, and $\zeta, \zeta' \in W$ with $\zeta\zeta' = 1$, $\zeta^n = 1$ and $\zeta^j - 1$ a unit of $W$ for all $0 < j < n$. Let $\theta$ be a $W$-algebra automorphism of $M$ whose $n$-fold iterate is the identity and which is diagonal to first order: $\theta(U) - \zeta U$ and $\theta(V) - \zeta' V$ lie in $\mathfrak m_M^2$. Let $M' =$ `UVCrossingModel W (π ^ (m * n))` and let $\psi \colon M' \to M$ be an injective ring homomorphism which is the identity on constants ($\psi(\mathrm{const}\,w) = \mathrm{const}\,w$ for all $w \in W$), which satisfies $\psi(U') = (\gamma U)^n$ and $\psi(V') = (\gamma' V)^n$ for some units $\gamma, \gamma'$ of $M$, and whose image is exactly the fixed set of $\theta$, i.e. $z \in \operatorname{range}\psi \iff \theta z = z$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions: for every $z \in M'$, every $e \in \mathbb N$ and every unit $w$ of $M$, if $\psi(z) = w\,V^e$ then $n \mid e$ and $z = w'\,V'^{\,e/n}$ for some unit $w'$ of $M'$; and the same with $U$, $U'$ in place of $V$, $V'$.
--
--   This is the exactness statement for monomial germs under a tame cyclic quotient of a crossing model: an invariant germ supported on one branch of the $\pi^m$-thick ordinary double point has exponent divisible by $n$ and descends to a monomial germ of exponent $e/n$ on the $\pi^{mn}$-thick crossing model, up to units. It is used in the per-node analysis of rigid charts on modular curves at full level, in the degree two and degree three cases of the Diamond argument and in the assembly of the rigid descent hypotheses.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_dvd_and_exists_eq_mul_pow_of_apply_eq_mul_pow_of_range_eq_fixedPoints.lean

